TinyUSB 0.21.0, audio device: re-arm the isochronous OUT endpoint after a
zero-length packet.

With a linear buffer (DMA mode on DWC2, where the endpoint has no dedicated
hardware FIFO), audiod_rx_xfer_isr() returns through TU_VERIFY when
tu_fifo_write_n() writes nothing, which it does for a zero-length packet,
before it re-arms the endpoint with usbd_edpt_xfer() and before it calls
tud_audio_rx_done_isr(). The endpoint then receives nothing until the host
selects an alt setting again. USB Audio Data Formats 2.0 (2.1, 2.3.1.5)
allows a zero-length packet, a transfer delimiter, in place of any packet,
and the function must handle it. This writes to the FIFO only when the
packet has data; the re-arm and the callback run as before.

Applied by firmware/CMakeLists.txt to a copy in the build folder; the
submodule stays at the release.

diff --git a/src/class/audio/audio_device.c b/src/class/audio/audio_device.c
--- a/src/class/audio/audio_device.c
+++ b/src/class/audio/audio_device.c
@@ -467,8 +467,11 @@
   uint8_t idx_audio_fct = audiod_get_audio_fct_idx(audio);
 
   #if !CFG_TUD_EDPT_DEDICATED_HWFIFO
-  // Data currently is in linear buffer, copy into EP OUT FIFO
-  TU_VERIFY(0 < tu_fifo_write_n(&audio->ep_out_ff, audio->lin_buf_out, n_bytes_received));
+  // Data currently is in linear buffer, copy into EP OUT FIFO. A zero-length packet has no data, but the endpoint
+  // must still be re-armed.
+  if (n_bytes_received > 0) {
+    TU_VERIFY(0 < tu_fifo_write_n(&audio->ep_out_ff, audio->lin_buf_out, n_bytes_received));
+  }
 
   // Schedule for next receive
   TU_VERIFY(usbd_edpt_xfer(rhport, audio->ep_out, audio->lin_buf_out, audio->ep_out_sz, true));
